  "notes": "{充|あ}てる means to allocate or assign something to a specific purpose. Written with {充|あ} to distinguish from other あてる verbs.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n\nKANJI DISTINCTIONS:\n- {充|あ}てる: to allocate, to assign (resources to a purpose)\n- {当|あ}てる: to hit, to guess, to apply\n- {宛|あ}てる: to address (a letter)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜を〜に{充|あ}てる: to assign X to Y\n- {予算|よさん}を{充|あ}てる: to allocate a budget\n- {時間|じかん}を{充|あ}てる: to devote time\n- {人員|じんいん}を{充|あ}てる: to assign personnel\n\nREGISTER:\nCommon in business, financial, and planning contexts. Slightly formal in tone.",
